{
    "uid": "aoc-d1-service-health",
    "title": "AOC / D1 Service Health (RED)",
    "tags": [
        "aoc",
        "red",
        "otel"
    ],
    "timezone": "browser",
    "schemaVersion": 39,
    "version": 1,
    "refresh": "30s",
    "time": {
        "from": "now-6h",
        "to": "now"
    },
    "templating": {
        "list": [
            {
                "name": "route",
                "label": "HTTP route",
                "type": "query",
                "datasource": {
                    "type": "prometheus",
                    "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
                },
                "query": "label_values(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{aoc_observation_type=\"http\"}, http_route)",
                "refresh": 2,
                "includeAll": true,
                "multi": true,
                "current": {
                    "text": "All",
                    "value": "$__all"
                },
                "allValue": ".*"
            }
        ]
    },
    "panels": [
        {
            "id": 1,
            "type": "text",
            "title": "How to read this dashboard",
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 4,
                "w": 24,
                "x": 0,
                "y": 0
            },
            "options": {
                "mode": "markdown",
                "content": "Every panel here is derived from spans by the Collector **spanmetrics** connector \u2014 there is no bespoke metrics instrumentation. HTTP panels carry **no tenant label** on purpose: `AuthContext` is a FastAPI dependency that is never written to `request.state`, and tenant x 170 API operations would dominate the series budget. Tenant-scoped signal lives in D2, D3 and D4.\n\n**If the *Collector health* row at the bottom is red, every other panel in every dashboard is lying.**"
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 2,
            "type": "timeseries",
            "title": "Request rate by route (req/s)",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 8,
                "w": 12,
                "x": 0,
                "y": 4
            },
            "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                    "unit": "reqps"
                },
                "overrides": []
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "sum by (http_route) (rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{aoc_observation_type=\"http\", http_route=~\"$route\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
                    "legendFormat": "{{http_route}}"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 3,
            "type": "timeseries",
            "title": "Error ratio by route (5xx / all)",
            "description": "Derived from aoc.http.status_class, which the HttpTelemetryMiddleware sets on every server span.",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 8,
                "w": 12,
                "x": 12,
                "y": 4
            },
            "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                    "unit": "percentunit",
                    "min": 0,
                    "max": 1
                },
                "overrides": []
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "sum by (http_route) (rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{aoc_observation_type=\"http\", aoc_http_status_class=\"5xx\", http_route=~\"$route\"}[$__rate_interval])) / clamp_min(sum by (http_route) (rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{aoc_observation_type=\"http\", http_route=~\"$route\"}[$__rate_interval])), 0.0001)",
                    "legendFormat": "{{http_route}}"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 4,
            "type": "timeseries",
            "title": "HTTP latency p50 / p95 / p99",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 8,
                "w": 12,
                "x": 0,
                "y": 12
            },
            "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                    "unit": "ms"
                },
                "overrides": []
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(traces_span_metrics_duration_milliseconds_bucket{aoc_observation_type=\"http\", http_route=~\"$route\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
                    "legendFormat": "p50"
                },
                {
                    "refId": "B",
                    "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(traces_span_metrics_duration_milliseconds_bucket{aoc_observation_type=\"http\", http_route=~\"$route\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
                    "legendFormat": "p95"
                },
                {
                    "refId": "C",
                    "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(traces_span_metrics_duration_milliseconds_bucket{aoc_observation_type=\"http\", http_route=~\"$route\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
                    "legendFormat": "p99"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 5,
            "type": "timeseries",
            "title": "Slowest routes (p95)",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 8,
                "w": 12,
                "x": 12,
                "y": 12
            },
            "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                    "unit": "ms"
                },
                "overrides": []
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "topk(10, histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, http_route) (rate(traces_span_metrics_duration_milliseconds_bucket{aoc_observation_type=\"http\"}[$__rate_interval]))))",
                    "legendFormat": "{{http_route}}"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 6,
            "type": "timeseries",
            "title": "Span error rate by observation type",
            "description": "Spans ending StatusCode.ERROR. Under the previous Langfuse adapter successful spans ended UNSET, so this split was impossible.",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 8,
                "w": 12,
                "x": 0,
                "y": 20
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "sum by (aoc_observation_type) (rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{status_code=\"STATUS_CODE_ERROR\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
                    "legendFormat": "{{aoc_observation_type}}"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 7,
            "type": "timeseries",
            "title": "Span throughput by observation type",
            "description": "Use this to confirm the repository sampling ratio is behaving. Repository spans are 176 of 300 instrumentation sites and are thinned by OTEL_SAMPLE_RATIO_REPOSITORY; event.* spans are dropped entirely at the Collector because they duplicate the execution_event table.",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 8,
                "w": 12,
                "x": 12,
                "y": 20
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "sum by (aoc_observation_type) (rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total[$__rate_interval]))",
                    "legendFormat": "{{aoc_observation_type}}"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 8,
            "type": "row",
            "title": "Collector health (meta-observability)",
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 1,
                "w": 24,
                "x": 0,
                "y": 28
            },
            "collapsed": false,
            "panels": []
        },
        {
            "id": 9,
            "type": "timeseries",
            "title": "Spans failed to export (0 is healthy)",
            "description": "Non-zero means traces are being dropped and every other panel understates reality. Uses 'or vector(0)' so a healthy pipeline renders 0 rather than 'No data', which is ambiguous on the panel whose whole job is to tell you the others are lying.",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 7,
                "w": 8,
                "x": 0,
                "y": 29
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "sum(rate(otelcol_exporter_send_failed_spans[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
                    "legendFormat": "failed spans/s"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 10,
            "type": "timeseries",
            "title": "Exporter queue size",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 7,
                "w": 8,
                "x": 8,
                "y": 29
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "sum by (exporter) (otelcol_exporter_queue_size) or vector(0)",
                    "legendFormat": "{{exporter}}"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 11,
            "type": "timeseries",
            "title": "Spans refused by the receiver (0 is healthy)",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "aoc-prometheus"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 7,
                "w": 8,
                "x": 16,
                "y": 29
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "sum(rate(otelcol_receiver_refused_spans[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
                    "legendFormat": "refused spans/s"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 12,
            "type": "row",
            "title": "Silent cost loss (Loki)",
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 1,
                "w": 24,
                "x": 0,
                "y": 36
            },
            "collapsed": false,
            "panels": []
        },
        {
            "id": 13,
            "type": "logs",
            "title": "Cost and rate-limit blind-spot events",
            "description": "These four named events are the only signal that spend or enforcement was silently lost. llm_usage_not_recorded and agent_run_turn_usage_not_recorded mean a paid model call produced no ledger row. 'Cache silent exception' means Redis failed and the rate limiter FAILED OPEN, which is a security condition, not just an observability one.",
            "datasource": {
                "type": "loki",
                "uid": "aoc-loki"
            },
            "gridPos": {
                "h": 10,
                "w": 24,
                "x": 0,
                "y": 37
            },
            "options": {
                "showTime": true,
                "wrapLogMessage": true,
                "sortOrder": "Descending"
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "expr": "{service_name=~\"agent-orchestration-core.*\"} |~ \"llm_usage_not_recorded|agent_run_turn_usage_not_recorded|agent_run_llm_turn_failed|Cache silent exception\""
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}
